DECISIONS:
  - Ticket says "19 functions in DESIGN.md §5"; §5 lists 17. Treated DESIGN.md as the
    frozen source and implemented exactly those 17; did not invent two more. Contract
    mismatch, not code drift.
  - isStateStale uses the §4.1 "5 s" floor as a fixed strict `>` threshold: age 5 is not
    stale, 6 is. §4.1's max(5 s, 3×poll) needs the poll interval, which the frozen
    one-argument signature does not carry; Panel.qml may apply a larger threshold.
  - Missing/negative age counts as stale (§4.1 + PRD F6: refuse writes rather than trust
    an unread timestamp). Missing rpm returns "—", never a false "0 rpm".
  - Fix strings use the commands DESIGN.md §8 documents verbatim
    (`systemctl restart afanctl`, `omafan-ctl status`); no sudo in the message.
